            <ArticleTitle>Pyridyl-Directed Cp*Rh(III)-Catalyzed B(3)-H Acyloxylation of o-Carborane.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>5178-5181</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b02450</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An efficient pyridyl-directed Rh(III)-catalyzed o-carborane B(3)-H acyloxylation is reported. The B(3)-H bond is the most electron-deficient vertex on o-carborane whose functionalization is challenging. The combination of Cu(OH)2 and diverse carboxylic acids provides low cost and abundant acyloxyl sources which could lead to moderate to excellent yields.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
